# Ponder pins drizzle-orm and kysely internally; no ponder release yet ships
# patched versions, and overriding them independently risks breaking ponder's
# ORM/query layer. All of these are SQL / JSON-path injection issues that require
# ATTACKER-CONTROLLED input reaching the query builder. An indexer only builds
# queries from its own developer-defined schema and on-chain events, never from
# untrusted request input, so they are not reachable in this context. They clear
# once ponder upgrades these deps (tracked separately as the ponder upgrade).

# drizzle-orm: SQL injection via improperly escaped SQL identifiers. Identifiers
# come from the indexer's own schema, not from untrusted input.
CVE-2026-39356

# kysely: SQL injection via unsanitized JSON path keys (requires Kysely<any> /
# silenced compile errors plus untrusted keys). Ponder builds its own typed queries.
CVE-2026-32763

# kysely: MySQL backslash-escaping SQL injection in sql.lit(). Ponder uses
# PostgreSQL/PGlite, not MySQL, and passes no untrusted sql.lit() input.
CVE-2026-33468

# kysely: JSON-path traversal injection via JSONPathBuilder.key()/.at(). Ponder
# never passes untrusted input to JSON-path builders.
CVE-2026-44635

# vite: server.fs.deny bypass on Windows alternate paths - a DEV-SERVER issue.
# The production indexer runs `ponder start`, never the vite dev server, and the
# image is Linux. Pinned via ponder's vite-node loader; not exploitable at runtime.
CVE-2026-53571
